meta {
  name: Space List Writers
  type: http
  seq: 159
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.listWriters?space=at:space/{{did}}/org.example.bucket/main&limit=100
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  space: at:space/{{did}}/org.example.bucket/main
  limit: 100
  ~cursor:
}

docs {
  The space host's writer set: every repo that has written into the space, each as its latest
  update. A "com.atproto.space.defs#repoWrite" carries the repoRev and data (commit digest) last
  reported for the repo and the spaceRev at which it last changed; a
  "com.atproto.space.defs#repoRemoved" carries only the spaceRev of its removal. This is the sync
  boundary, not an access-control list — it enumerates writers, never readers, and a member who
  has only ever read is absent. Taken-down writers are listed like any other.

  For a repo hosted elsewhere the repoRev/data come from that host's notifyRepoUpdate and may lag;
  the repo's own host is the source of truth. Syncers use this to heal anything the best-effort
  notifications missed: entries are in ascending spaceRev order, prevSpaceRev is never set, and
  the cursor is a spaceRev (exclusive), so resume from the last one seen.

  Answered only by the space's authority. A space this server merely keeps repos in reads as
  400 SpaceNotFound — ask its authority instead. A taken-down or deactivated authority answers
  400 RepoTakendown / RepoDeactivated. Auth: a space credential, or the authority's own session.
}
